   "q": "What makes a good prompt for Claude?",
   "hint": "Think of briefing a brilliant new colleague who knows nothing about your project.",
   "answer": "A good prompt is clear and direct: it says what to do, why, who it is for, what good output looks like and in what format. It adds context the model cannot guess, gives 3 to 5 examples when the format matters, and separates instructions from data with XML tags.",
   "explain": "<p>The test from the prompting guide: show the prompt to a colleague with no context. If they would be confused, Claude will be too. Explaining the reason behind a rule (\"no ellipses because a text to speech engine reads this\") works better than shouting the rule in capitals.</p>",
