   "q": "What is context rot and how do you design around it?",
   "hint": "More tokens is not always better.",
   "answer": "Context rot is the drop in recall and precision as the context window fills up, because attention is spread over more tokens. Treat context as a limited budget: keep only high signal information, load details just in time with tools, compact long histories, keep structured notes outside the window, and hand large searches to subagents that return short summaries.",
   "explain": "<p>Context engineering asks \"what is the smallest set of high signal tokens that gets the outcome\". It is the step after prompt engineering for agents that run many turns.</p>",
